    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div><br>Il giorno martedì 12 febbraio 2019 09:29:42 UTC+1, Eric Rexstad ha scritto:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Emiliano</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>I assume you are making use of the methods described in the paper </div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>Howe, Eric J., Stephen T. Buckland, Marie-Lyne Després‐Einspenner, and Hjalmar S. Kühl. 2017. Distance Sampling with Camera Traps.\r\n<em>Methods in Ecology and Evolution</em> 8 (11): 1558–65. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12790\" title=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12790\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12790&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mFH_nRd00lL1fKrkkCPCA\">\r\nhttps://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12790</a>.</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>The authors of that paper have provided their data in a repository described at the end of the paper: \r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>&quot;The data files from which densities of Maxwell’s duikers were estimated using Distance software, and data describing start times of videos  of Maxwell’s duikers, have been archived at the Dryad data repository (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QUhfDCdEcSARa6lNbbiwT\">https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad</a>. b4c70) (Howe\r\n et al. 2017).&quot;</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>If you visit that repository link, they provide their data, as well as a description of the data, where I think you will find your answer regarding how effort was calculated:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>&quot;Filmed Maxwell&#39;s duikers were assigned to distance intervals; recorded distances are the midpoints of the intervals. &quot;Sample.Label&quot; references the trap location. &quot;Effort&quot; is temporal effort, i.e. the number of 2-second time-steps over which the camera\r\n operated. &quot;multiplier&quot; describes spatial effort, as the proportion of a circle covered by the angle of view of the camera. The data is formatted as a &quot;flatfile&quot; suitable for use with distance sampling software including Distance and associated R packages.&quot;</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>I hope this is helpful.</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/vDrBpGXFsygeD6T1xYhgxGTyLAH4OSUswdGwkYjItFVNKoDItnfuJUmP5ELFwHcMp2A3cJDQKL17uo2pxxxzYTbLAPxhRlrPfqOlE1-DdpgEYwL0Z_qyJFLySe7WLllNiUWTCZPH84xyjx9suwj8GMQ_qTbghm59s0f6sBhZBUlgLSWtSejw_eOZVcMD4sc1PzOWGNVv_z49vMq9hrcMusQGgvW2vkauW26NX3kJOywgZAI5Jgrxou4ok8QZ=w5000-h5000\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" style=\"max-width:60px;max-height:60px;margin-right:10px\"></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>Eric Rexstad</div>\r\n<div>Senior Research Fellow, CREEM, Univ. of St Andrews, Charity SC013532</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:0.9em;border-top:1px solid gray;min-width:250px;max-width:300px;margin-top:4px;padding-top:4px\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div><a rel=\"nofollow\">eric.r...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"margin-right:8px\"><a rel=\"nofollow\">+44 (0)1334 461833</a></span></div>\r\n<div><a href=\"https://maps.google.com/?q=The%20Observatory%2C%20Buchanan%20Gardens%2C%20St%20Andrews%20KY16%209LZ\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://maps.google.com/?q%3DThe%2520Observatory%252C%2520Buchanan%2520Gardens%252C%2520St%2520Andrews%2520KY16%25209LZ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2znfUlAlbAPisjXsOQaohi\">The Observatory, Buchanan Gardens, St Andrews KY16 9LZ</a></div>\r\n<div><a href=\"http://erex.github.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://erex.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw35W083fSKaw9rnbvtf9YK_\">http://erex.github.io</a></div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>On Feb 12 2019, at 8:15 am, Emiliano Manzo &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">emilian...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Hi Distance users,</font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"> </font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">I have a question about effort calculation when it’s used with camera traps as a point transect</font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I have to calculate the effort for a project using 21 traps for 15 days in each point active for 24 h per day, i have\r\n set up the traps for 20 seconds video with a delay of 2 sec. The detection angle 0.733RAD.</font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">What is confusing me is if I have to calculate the effort for 24 h at each point or only the time when I shot the video\r\n of my target species</font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Any suggestion for the calculation?</font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Thank for any clarification</font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Best</font></font></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\"><font style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><font style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Emiliano</font></font></font></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>--</div>\r\n<div>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.</div>\r\n<div>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a title=\"mailto:distance-sampling+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\ndistance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.</div>\r\n<div>To post to this group, send email to <a title=\"mailto:distance-sampling@googlegroups.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\ndistance...@googlegroups.com</a>.</div>\r\n<div>To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/298947c0-fa30-4943-8f95-ed05c4e06b70%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" title=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/298947c0-fa30-4943-8f95-ed05c4e06b70%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/298947c0-fa30-4943-8f95-ed05c4e06b70%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XVxhtez0dL3duKGLS3-x_\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/298947c0-fa30-4943-8f95-ed05c4e06b70%40googlegroups.com</a>.</div>\r\n<div>For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" title=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474211948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RYGL_SBDXoh3DqqLzM665\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div>"
