  {
   "id": "swMvRWryAgAJ",
   "from": "ej...@st-andrews.ac.uk",
   "author": "9c6614a1b3d9e242",
   "date": "2019-02-14T00:31:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: Sample Effort with camera Traps",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Emiliano,<div><br></div><div>I think of temporal sampling effort as the number of opportunities (in time) to record distances to animals. We defined temporal sampling effort at one CT location as the total duration of sampling at that location, divided by the length of the time step between the predetermined &quot;snapshot moments&quot; at which distances are recorded. So, if the CT operates for one hour (Tk = 3600 seconds), and we record distance at 2-second intervals (t = 2), then temporal effort is Tk / t = 3600 / 2.</div><div><br></div><div>The fact that CTs observe less than a complete circle can be included in your estimate of &quot;Effort&quot; at a location by dividing the horizontal angle of view of the camera in radians (&quot;theta&quot;), by a 2*pi (radians in a complete circle).  Combining Tk / 2 (temporal effort) and theta / 2*pi (spatial effort &lt; a complete circle) yields the definition of effort presented in the article ( theta * Tk / 2*pi*t.)</div><div><br></div><div>Alternatively, you can use &quot;Effort&quot; (in Distance) to define temporal effort only, and use theta / 2*pi as a &quot;multiplier&quot;. This is the approach we took with the duiker analysis. </div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Eric</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Tuesday, 12 February 2019 03:15:48 UTC-5, Emiliano Manzo  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hi Distance\r\nusers,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I have a\r\nquestion about effort calculation when it’s used with camera traps as a point\r\ntransect</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;layout-grid-mode:both\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I have\r\nto calculate the effort for a project using 21 traps for\r\n15 days in each point active for 24 h per day, i have set up the traps for 20\r\nseconds video with a delay of 2 sec. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">The detection angle 0.733</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">RAD.</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">What is\r\nconfusing me is if I have to calculate the effort for 24 h at each point or\r\nonly the time when I shot the video of my target species</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Any\r\nsuggestion for the calculation?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Thank for any clarification</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Best</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Emiliano</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
